## Final like-for-like timing (one session: 2026-10-27 12:01, host eu-g6-048, commit d57fdf6)

Same 200 LIGYSIS chains for every tool (`baselines/ligysis_speed200.txt`, median 1,803 atoms), same node (AMD EPYC 9554, 4x RTX 4090), measured back to back by `scripts/bench_final.py`; nothing else of this project ran on the node. **Shared node:** other users' jobs ran concurrently. Node load (1/5/15 min) is given for every measurement. BURROW = the CLI default models for each preset with the `all` ranker (fast: `results/dev/freeze_fast`, default/accurate: `results/dev/freeze_v2`), fast backend, BLAS/Numba pinned to 1 thread per process.

| method | 1 core warm, excl. parsing: median / p90 ms | 1 core warm, incl. parsing: median / p90 ms | 1 process on 200 chains, wall s (amortised ms; start-up incl.) | 24 CPU workers, structures/s | 1 GPU (8 workers), structures/s | 3 GPUs (8 workers each), structures/s |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| BURROW fast | 31.4 / 75.1 | 41.6 / 100.2 | 12.6 (63) | 214.2 | 129.1 | 177.3 |
| BURROW default | 99.3 / 271.3 | 110.6 / 296.8 | 31.3 (156) | 123.2 | 96.6 | 162.4 |
| BURROW accurate | 205.7 / 500.4 | 216.8 / 528.2 | 57.6 (288) | 72.6 | 77.5 | 141.0 |

Loads (1/5/15 min) per measurement: BURROW fast 1-core 25.23 26.21 27.75 -> 24.35 25.99 27.66; BURROW default 1-core 24.35 25.99 27.66 -> 40.66 29.63 28.81; BURROW accurate 1-core 40.66 29.63 28.81 -> 39.13 31.60 29.56; cpu1w fast 39.13 31.60 29.56 -> 35.05 31.06 29.42; cpuN fast 24.51 28.35 28.59 -> 28.91 29.18 28.86; gpu1 fast 35.91 30.98 29.48 -> 33.55 30.69 29.41; gpu3 fast 29.32 29.91 29.20 -> 28.94 29.80 29.18; cpuN_large fast 30.82 30.18 29.32 -> 34.41 31.08 29.64; gpu3_large fast 38.88 35.15 31.52 -> 39.72 35.58 31.74; cpu1w default 35.05 31.06 29.42 -> 28.71 29.91 29.09; cpuN default 28.91 29.18 28.86 -> 31.80 29.81 29.07; gpu1 default 33.55 30.69 29.41 -> 30.92 30.26 29.30; gpu3 default 28.94 29.80 29.18 -> 31.20 30.25 29.33; cpuN_large default 34.41 31.08 29.64 -> 37.77 32.82 30.35; gpu3_large default 39.72 35.58 31.74 -> 38.26 35.54 31.84; cpu1w accurate 28.71 29.91 29.09 -> 24.51 28.35 28.59; cpuN accurate 31.80 29.81 29.07 -> 35.91 30.98 29.48; gpu1 accurate 30.92 30.26 29.30 -> 29.32 29.91 29.20; gpu3 accurate 31.20 30.25 29.33 -> 30.82 30.18 29.32; cpuN_large accurate 37.77 32.82 30.35 -> 38.88 35.15 31.52; gpu3_large accurate 38.26 35.54 31.84 -> 38.11 35.78 32.07.

Columns: *1 core warm* = per-structure wall time in one warm process (first structure run twice before timing), excl. or incl. reading/parsing the PDB file; *1 process on 200 chains* = complete CLI run with one worker (`python -m pocketdetect.burrow.fast predict --workers 1`; interpreter start, imports, model load, parsing, writing) and, for the baselines, the project wrappers with the same input list (P2Rank: gemmi cleaning + one JVM over all 200 files, JVM start included; fpocket: gemmi cleaning + one fpocket process per structure, sequential); throughput columns = speed200 x 10 (2,000 structures) through the BURROW CLI incl. parsing and writing, process start-up included. Baseline per-structure medians: P2Rank batch mode gives only the amortised time (JVM total / 200); fpocket's column is the fpocket call per structure (it includes fpocket's own parsing), gemmi cleaning median – ms in addition. Multi-thread baseline numbers (P2Rank 8/32 threads 49/47 ms, fpocket 32 processes 39 ms per structure) are from the earlier session in results/baselines/SPEED.md (load 20-68).

